[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit, 4.d4"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pawn-grab"]
[Themes "centre-fight,open-e-file"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.d4"]
[Start "rousseau-gambit 3...f5"]

4. d4 { Strikes at the centre at once. The engine rates this as good for White as 4.d3, so Black needs to know the answers. } 4... exd4 { Takes the pawn and opens the e-file. White still stands better, but Black has real counterplay and no weak king squares yet. } 5. e5 ( 5. Ng5 Ne5 { Attacks the bishop and fights for the centre while the knight on g5 has no support. } 6. Bxg8 Rxg8 7. Qxd4 d6 ) ( 5. O-O fxe4 { Wins a second pawn while White spends a move castling. } 6. Nxd4 d5 { Hits the bishop and opens the c8 bishop. } 7. Nxc6 bxc6 ) 5... d5 { Hits the bishop and the pawn chain. If the bishop moves away, ...Bb4+ or ...dxe5 follows with a good game. } 6. exd6 ( 6. Bb5 Bb4+ { Checks and pulls the c-pawn forward, so ...dxc3 opens lines against White's king. } 7. c3 dxc3 8. bxc3 Bc5 ) 6... cxd6 { Recaptures with the c-pawn, which keeps the queen at home and lets Black's pawns march ...d5 next. } 7. O-O d5 { Hits the bishop again and takes the centre. Black is down about a pawn and a half here, the price of this gambit: develop with ...Nf6, castle, and win the d4 pawn back before you open the f-file. } *
